+## 2026-10-24 radius-cap curriculum repair
+
+A protected-Racket probe found a concrete lesson shortcut in version 2.0.0: seed 47, easy samples 0–1 both had maximum local motif radius 2, while query sample 2 required radius 3. Replacing the canonical extraction radius with 2 matched both demonstrations and failed the query (`checks/efa31853b924/radius-shortcut.json`).
+
+Version 2.1.0 now anchors a radius-3 offset on every even sample index, so every two consecutive demonstrations contain a direct counterexample to that shortcut without increasing the demo budget. The fallback follows the same parity contract. A new regression sweeps 576 generated examples across all bands, and the retained curriculum probe covers 60 two-demo lessons / 180 examples plus three protected-Racket radius-2 rival checks. All repaired checks pass (`checks/efa31853b924-tests/result.json`, `checks/efa31853b924/radius-curriculum.json`).
+
+Limit: this repair directly closes the radius-2 cap; it is not an exhaustive identifiability proof for every local-frame shortcut. Owner integration remains pending under the optional-peer policy.
